<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gulussa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gulussa was a Numidian prince, a son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a>. On his father's death in 148 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-aemilianus">Scipio Aemilianus</a> divided the royal functions among the three legitimate sons, and Gulussa received command of the army, which he led on the Roman side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-punic-war">Third Punic War</a>. He died before his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/micipsa">Micipsa</a>, and his son Massiva was later murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a>'s orders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gulussa.jpg" alt="Gulussa" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pi%C3%A8ce_de_Gulussa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
